<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhang Fei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 221</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhang Fei was a general of the late Han and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, a companion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bei">Liu Bei</a> from the start of his career together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guan-yu">Guan Yu</a>. Famed for his courage and fierce temper, he held the bridge at Changban in 208 to cover Liu Bei's retreat. He was murdered by his own officers in 221 as Shu prepared to attack Wu.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhang-fei.jpg" alt="Zhang Fei" width="320" height="358" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: White whirlwind · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zhang_Fei_(Chinese_characters).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
